      {
        "id": 222308,
        "name": "Gus_Smedstad",
        "username": "Gus_Smedstad",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/e8c25b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-20T17:40:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Blackfang108\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Blackfang108:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>in my replay, not a single Agent was killed, and they were complete nonentities.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That’s surprising.</p>\n<p>We start with Battle Medic, who makes it more difficult to kill Steel since he heals Steel every turn. I seem to recall the order was Infiltrator, Sharpshooter, Bomb Specialist. WIth Battle Medic still around, Infiltrator adds another card play for Steel, Sharpshooter does little, and Bomb Specialist adds 2 fire damage to Steel’s attacks.</p>\n<p>2 healing per turn for Steel is somewhat important. Infilitrator’s going to turn up at least one additional negative card, though I don’t recall his one-shots in this game. If you kill Steel fast enough Bomb Specialist won’t come out, so I can see her not qualifying.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:55:12.713Z",
